# Evaluation-area rules

- No universal virality score, ever: rubrics are multidimensional; evaluation reports carry
  per-check results and an overall pass/pass_with_warnings/fail — not a number.
- Every evaluation report must fill `cannot_validate_without_real_data` honestly.
- Fixtures are a fixed benchmark set: changing an existing fixture invalidates historical
  comparisons, so prefer adding fixtures; edits to existing ones need explicit justification in
  the PR.
- Regression rule: on any skill version bump, run old and new against the same fixtures, record
  material differences under `evaluation/regression/`, and have the skill critic name both
  improvements and regressions. Newer or longer output is not presumed better.
- Rubric changes are PR-gated like skills (they are evaluation policy).
- Structural validity: `python3 tools/run_fixtures.py` and
  `python3 tools/validate_artifacts.py` must pass.
